      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Source-backed Gateway; external Native contract",
      "items": [
        "Nodes cite Gateway's Native consumer boundary, not Native implementation in this repository. Repository metadata must identify Root's real Git source checkpoint before rendering.",
        "Normal scope selection needs no resolve_project alias. Browsing and get_capabilities are passive; first task preparation may initialize the owned root through existing guarded phases. Current token scopes, owner policy, connection, root and credential are rechecked. Setup never bypasses fleet restore or grants general administration. Legacy alias pins and physical-binding semantics remain separate; Native root, credential and process identities keep their strict guards.",
        "prepare_dispatch resolves its stable client key before current paths, connectivity or random IDs. It freezes operation/task identity, selector and literal Native options with omission preserved. prepare_continuation binds one successor to the exact predecessor operation/task/spec/request and same Native context; omitted selection, brief and options inherit. Only budget/model/effort/output-silence overrides are accepted; Native alone decides continuation eligibility. dispatch_task confirms the retained draft; changed replay input conflicts.",
        "Native alone validates/defaults providers, models, effort, permissions, budgets and timeouts, and owns admission, sessions, lifecycle and accepted results. list_models explicitly obtains dated advisory facts; cached discovery cannot veto execution intent. New routing requires negotiated Native execution-option, project-hash and immutable Origin-binding support; continuation also requires its guarded feature. Missing support is an upgrade error."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "No synthetic task closure",
      "items": [
        "Rows are related procedures, not automatic transitions. Lost ACK, timeout, disconnect, accepted result bytes and cancellation requested do not prove task closure. Unknown transmitted work retains its execution reservation. Session owners join parent-cancellation hooks before reporting done. Expected SDK shutdown requires qualified Serve cancellation and clean Close; it proves neither task closure nor a successful connection.",
        "Explicit cancellation first sends Gateway FenceAbsent for the original ID. A complete matching existing receipt is resolved passively, without Native refusal locking, and may then be canceled. Only validated absence or independently root-checked partial preparation invokes the Native refusal fence. Unknown or partial evidence retains the reservation.",
        "Execution reservation release requires validated canonical execution closure, an exact requested-and-terminated stop, or permanent refusal. Result bytes and routing completion do not establish task closure.",
        "Revoked principal/grant/device or stale credential/connection blocks current sends and responses. Already-transmitted work can finish; revocation is not task cancellation.",
        "Saved task controls use immutable root/project/Origin guards after path or approval removal. Existing-only recovery still validates the canonical receipt/spec and current authority. A removed approval cannot authorize new selection or admission; the connector does not rebind historical tasks to current directories."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Recovery conserves identity and visibility",
      "items": [
        "Full prior-fleet coverage precedes EVERY routed CLI. Out-of-band operator CLI-only join attestation is frozen to device, credential, boot and exact generation; it does not establish Native task closure.",
        "Persist barriers before inventory. Compact Origin binding restores original request keys, exact task correlations and permanent refusal tombstones, including typed predecessor identity. Invalid/noncanonical/wrong-owner binding rejects the whole page without advancing progress. Legacy missing-binding imports retain their historical rules. Attributed and unattributed records share one ledger; unowned work remains admin-only.",
        "Missing coverage, mapping, completeness, regular credential or reopen revision keeps recovery blocked. Recovery-only permits observation/cancel/fence/barrier/inventory after routing coverage, never admit/resume/reopen. Fresh root proof follows reopen before Registry finish.",
        "Raw requested options have one authority: the retained Gateway request body. Compact rows and binding-present wire inventory carry no second options copy. After body disposal, stable replay and historical observation/cancel/fence/existing-only recovery remain possible; fresh admission is forbidden. Refusal supplies no invented spec, receipt, result or closure. Native inventory membership/hash bytes stay canonical."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Two independent resource ledgers",
      "items": [
        "Execution reservations account for uncertain Native work; new scope-relative execution admission belongs to Native. Legacy aliases retain Gateway legacy execution quotas. Routing permits bound Gateway-routed CLI owners independently of task budgets, operator CLI/SSH/TUI and local startup probes.",
        "Routing completion is not task completion. Keep permits while CLI Wait/output copiers/owned cleanup remain unresolved. Same-process fenced census or protected explicit drain can settle prior controls; socket closure alone cannot.",
        "Retention preserves the phase-4 rule: only closed routing rows older than the current generation compact. Active owners, execution reservations and canonical task evidence are not released by compaction. Schema 10 removes obsolete execution-policy ceilings only through explicit migration, preserving frozen legacy operation bytes."
      ]
    },
